sor score.** Before the FIRST code write, route through `sk-code`. Before the FIRST `.md` write, route through `sk-doc`, except spec-folder docs (`system-spec-kit`'s) and the gitignored runtime state Gate 3 exempts, which no skill owns. Routing means loading what its ROUTER.md resolves, per Gate 5's loading rule. A skill already in context is not re-read. A resolved contract wrong for this case is followed and amended, per PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK step 4.\n70: - Output: `SKILL ROUTING: [result]` or `SKILL ROUTING: User directed → [name]`; when the artifact trigger fires, add `ARTIFACT: [skill] → [what its router resolved]`\n71: - Skip: trivial queries only (greetings, single-line questions). The artifact trigger skips only the §6 exemption class.\n72: \n73: #### GATE 3: SPEC FOLDER QUESTION [HARD] BLOCK — ASKED FIRST\n74: **Fires when** the turn will write a file — creating, editing, deleting, moving, or generating one — or will write continuity state (a save, a resume, a further iteration). **Does not fire** when the request is purely read-only: review, audit, inspect, analyze, explain, standing alone, or when its only write is gitignored runtime state under `.skilled/skills/.state/`. A read-only word next to a write trigger does not disqualify it.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 75]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/AGENTS.md, lines 55-74\n55: \n56: | Confidence | Action |\n57: | --- | --- |\n58: | **≥80%** | Proceed with citable source |\n59: | **40-79%** | Proceed with caveats |\n60: | **<40%** | Ask for clarification or mark \"UNKNOWN\" |\n61: | **Override** | Blockers/conflicts → ask regardless of score |\n62: \n63: #### GATE 2: SKILL ROUTING [REQUIRED for non-trivial tasks]\n64: 1. A) Primary: use the Skill Advisor Hook brief the runtime surfaced, when present. See `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md`.\n65: 2. B) Direct call: run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"[request]\"}' --format json` when no hook brief is present or when diagnosing hook behavior.\n66: 3. C) Cite user's explicit direction: \"User specified: [exact quote]\"\n67: - Confidence ≥ 0.8 → MUST invoke skill | < 0.8 → general approach | User names skill → cite and proceed\n68: - **Command in the brief.** A brief or advisor result that names a command offers its workflow beside the skill's. Take either path whole, never an improvised one. To take the command, read its document in full and follow it. `run` starts it now. `start` starts it without `:auto`, so its setup asks. `ask` offers it in one question and waits. A typed command or explicit instruction outranks the policy. Output: `COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]`\n69: - **Artifact trigger — binds on what you write, regardless of the advisor score.** Before the FIRST code write, route through `sk-code`. Before the FIRST `.md` write, route through `sk-doc`, except spec-folder docs (`system-spec-kit`'s) and the gitignored runtime state Gate 3 exempts, which no skill owns. Routing means loading what its ROUTER.md resolves, per Gate 5's loading rule. A skill already in context is not re-read. A resolved contract wrong for this case is followed and amended, per PLAN-WORKFLOW LOCK step 4.\n70: - Output: `SKILL ROUTING: [result]` or `SKILL ROUTING: User directed → [name]`; when the artifact trigger fires, add `ARTIFACT: [skill] → [what its router resolved]`\n71: - Skip: trivial queries only (greetings, single-line questions). The artifact trigger skips only the §6 exemption class.\n72: \n73: #### GATE 3: SPEC FOLDER QUESTION [HARD] BLOCK — ASKED FIRST\n74: **Fires when** the turn will write a file — creating, editing, deleting, moving, or generating one — or will write continuity state (a save, a resume, a further iteration). **Does not fire** when the request is purely read-only: review, audit, inspect, analyze, explain, standing alone, or when its only write is gitignored runtime state under `.skilled/skills/.state/`. A read-only word next to a write trigger does not disqualify it.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 75]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/AGENTS.md\", \"offset\": 55, \"limit\": 20}"},"time":{"start":1794584631382,"end":1794584632749}}}}
